      "writtenOn": "2023-01-26T19:01:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\"standard library\" is common terminology to pretty much all programming languages. So I think stdlib or standardLibrary is the correct name for this.\n\nHere\u0027s some python documentation that uses that terminology: https://docs.python.org/3/library/\nRust uses it too: https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/\nGo: https://pkg.go.dev/std\n\nJava is an outlier here in that I can\u0027t find the words \"standard library\" in their docs.",
      "parentUuid": "87741fa9_9411f619",
