        "id": 1535516
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-26T19:01:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The problem with that is that `NamedTemporaryFile` opens the file for read/writing. So if we moved all the code in the `with` blocks, we\u0027d at least have to flush the input file after writing it, but I also preferred not to have the file opened by both this script and `py_compile` at the same time.\n\nI like having the prefix so that if the file isn\u0027t deleted for some reason, you can see what the file was for. When it\u0027s just random characters it\u0027s hard to know if it\u0027s a file that\u0027s being used or not. But I don\u0027t feel too strong about this.",
      "parentUuid": "b9dc6efb_c851a186",
      "range": {
